WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.640
All right friends.

00:04.640 --> 00:06.960
So now let's have a quick recap about views.

00:06.960 --> 00:13.320
So we have learned that views are a virtual table that is based on the result of a query without actually

00:13.320 --> 00:15.360
storing any data in the database.

00:15.360 --> 00:21.600
So we use views in order to persist a complex SQL logic and query in the database.

00:21.600 --> 00:27.960
And we have learned that in some scenarios, views are better than CTE because it improves their reusability

00:27.960 --> 00:34.280
and reduce the complexity in multiple queries, which reduce the complexity of the whole project, where

00:34.280 --> 00:37.760
the CTE only improves the reusability in one query.

00:37.760 --> 00:39.240
And we have learned that as well.

00:39.240 --> 00:41.840
The views in some scenarios are better than tables.

00:41.840 --> 00:47.600
We have learned that they are very flexible and easier to maintain since they don't store any data,

00:47.600 --> 00:52.120
and it's really fast and easy to change stuff in the view compared to the tables.

00:52.120 --> 00:57.440
But as will we have learned that the tables are faster than views now, they are like endless use cases

00:57.440 --> 01:01.920
for the views, but from my experience in projects, I have choose for you the best use cases for the

01:01.920 --> 01:02.440
views.

01:02.480 --> 01:10.240
The first use case is if we find like a common repeated logic in SQL queries, we can go and store this

01:10.240 --> 01:16.130
logic in a view in the database so that the users don't have to keep repeating the logic over and over.

01:16.130 --> 01:19.770
So we use views in order to have a central business logic.

01:19.810 --> 01:25.530
Another use case is to hide the complexity of your physical data model and to offer for the users a

01:25.530 --> 01:26.930
high abstracted layer.

01:26.930 --> 01:32.450
So you provide for the user something very friendly, and you hide all the complex technical data model

01:32.450 --> 01:36.690
that you have in the database, because not everyone is expert with your data model.

01:36.730 --> 01:37.490
One more use case.

01:37.490 --> 01:42.930
We can use views in order to implement security and to protect our sensitive data in the database,

01:42.930 --> 01:48.010
so we can offer multiple views in order to protect columns or rows in a table.

01:48.050 --> 01:48.730
Another use case.

01:48.730 --> 01:55.010
We have learned that we can use views in order to have more dynamic and flexibility for your database,

01:55.010 --> 02:00.210
where we offer the users a stable view, and then you have the freedom to change stuff at your physical

02:00.210 --> 02:02.970
data model without affecting all users.

02:02.970 --> 02:05.170
And another nice use case for the views.

02:05.170 --> 02:11.210
We can offer multiple languages from our data model, and the last use case, we have learned how views

02:11.250 --> 02:14.530
play an important role in a data warehouse system.

02:14.530 --> 02:15.970
So views are amazing.

02:16.010 --> 02:16.730
All right my friends.

02:16.730 --> 02:21.210
So with that we have learned everything about this new objects, the views in databases.

02:21.210 --> 02:24.330
This is amazing for flexibility and dynamic in your projects.

02:24.370 --> 02:28.130
Now in the next one we are going to learn how to create tables based on query.

02:28.130 --> 02:30.650
And we will learn about the temporary tables.

02:30.650 --> 02:31.330
So let's go.
